  "prior_findings": "Measured on a trained version of the template module (success about 0.73-0.79 of episodes): of ALL episodes, about 7.8% fail without the module ever firing (mostly the pen is dropped before step 60); about 7.2% fire and roll again but are not rolling steadily (above 4 rad/s, centred) when the blend and the 60 boost steps have ended, and mostly finish persistently slow; about 3.2% fire and never roll again (a third of them drop the pen late); about 1.6% roll steadily at the end of the blend or boost and lose it within 30 steps. An earlier study found that a second attempt added nothing over simply training the single attempt longer, and that small fixed joint offsets during the first 60 steps added nothing. Performance falls sharply when the pen starts from a wider range of reset poses. Without any module the root controller succeeds in about 0.55 of episodes and about 41% of episodes roll persistently slowly (about 2 rad/s).",
